┌─────────────────────────────── Game Concept ────────────────────────────────┐
│ The Midnight Interchange                                                    │
│ A single moonlit train station suspended between worlds, where the 12:00    │
│ train never quite arrives and three puzzle spirits drift between five       │
│ brass-and-glass rooms. Each night the clockmaker, Wren Tallow, must repair  │
│ the station's failing mechanisms before the moon sets.                      │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
  Regions: The Midnight Interchange
  Items: 11 created
  Quests: 6  |  NPCs: 5
  Style: Hand-pixeled 2D at a 64x64 sprite base for characters and key props, 
with 32x32 tile units for floors/walls and 128x128 reserved for hero set-pieces
(Arrival Clock, Workshop Ledger floor, Great Skylight). Target render 
resolution: 384x216 internal canvas upscaled 5x to 1920x1080 with integer 
scaling, no sub-pixel filtering. Sprites use a strict 24-color global palette 
per scene with selective dithering (Bayer 4x4) only on glass and steam edges. 
Character silhouettes read at 3 tiles tall (Wren ~40px), with brass-loupe and 
apron-buckle as silhouette anchors. Animations: 8-frame idle breathing loops at
8fps, 6-frame winding loops at 12fps, 4-frame pendulum sways at 6fps, 12-frame 
steam puffs at 10fps for parallax layers, and 24-frame moon-meter sweep cycles 
tied to the 12-minute timer. UI is ink-on-aged-paper: hand-drawn at 2x pixel 
scale with 1px sepia outlines (#3a2a1c), drop-shadowed onto a paper texture 
overlay set to multiply at 35% opacity. Lantern bloom is achieved with a 3-pass
additive blur on amber light sources (radius 2px, 4px, 8px) clamped to a 50% 
alpha ceiling so it never crushes the palette. Two parallax steam layers move 
at 0.25x and 0.6x camera speed; foreground gear-shadows pass at 1.4x. No 
anti-aliasing on sprite edges; all rotations are pre-baked at 8 cardinal angles
to preserve the hand-pixeled feel.
┌───────────────────────────────── QA Report ─────────────────────────────────┐
